  ## 2. ISO/IEC 27001 & ISMS Fundamentals

  ### Q4: "What is ISO/IEC 27001 and what is an ISMS?"

  │ Answer:
  │ "ISO/IEC 27001 is the international standard for managing information security. It specifies the requirements for establishing, implementing, maintaining, and
  │ continually improving an Information Security Management System (ISMS).
  │ An ISMS is a systematic framework of policies, procedures, and technical controls designed to manage sensitive company data and protect the CIA Triad
  │ (Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability) using a risk-based approach."

  ### Q5: "What is the difference between ISO 27001 Mandatory Clauses (4 to 10) and Annex A Controls?"

  │ Answer:
  │
  │ • Mandatory Clauses (4–10): Define how the management system operates:
  │     • Clause 4: Context of the Organization
  │     • Clause 5: Leadership & Commitment
  │     • Clause 6: Planning (Risk Assessment & Objectives)
  │     • Clause 7: Support (Resources, Competence, Awareness)
  │     • Clause 8: Operation (Execution of risk assessments and controls)
  │     • Clause 9: Performance Evaluation (Internal Audit & Management Review)
  │     • Clause 10: Improvement (Non-conformities & Corrective Actions)
  │ • Annex A: A catalog of specific security controls organizations select to mitigate risks identified in Clause 6.

  ### Q6: "What changed between ISO 27001:2013 and ISO 27001:2022?"

  │ Answer:
  │ "ISO 27001:2022 modernized and restructured the controls:
  │
  │ 1. Controls were consolidated from 114 controls across 14 domains down to 93 controls across 4 themes:
  │     • Organizational (37 controls)
  │     • People (8 controls)
  │     • Physical (14 controls)
  │     • Technological (34 controls)
  │ 2. Introduced 11 brand-new controls, including Threat Intelligence, Cloud Security, Web Filtering, Data Masking, Data Leakage Prevention (DLP), and Monitoring
  │ Activities.
  │ 3. Added metadata attributes (Control Types, Cybersecurity Concepts, Operational Capabilities) to make tracking easier."
  ### Q7: "What is a Statement of Applicability (SoA)?"
  │ Answer:
  │ "The Statement of Applicability (SoA) is one of the most critical documents in ISO 27001. It lists all 93 controls from Annex A, states whether each control is
  │ applicable or excluded, explains the justification for inclusion or exclusion, and describes how the applicable controls are implemented."
